{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/200712-something-i-noticed-in-the-on-the-horizon-section-of-the-onyx-path-release-list","id":200712,"title":"Something I noticed in the 'on the horizon' section of the Onyx Path release list","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-17T21:33:51-07:00","id":200712,"title":"Something I noticed in the 'on the horizon' section of the Onyx Path release list","content":"I don't know the best way to ask this or indeed if I should ask this here or whatever or if I'll ever get an answer, but I noticed a new Geist product in development. I was wondering if this meant we'd be getting an update to geist to the GMC rules anytime in the foreseeable future or if we're forever stuck as the littlest gameline in WoD. <br /> <br /> For that matter, if we got a GMC update, would we get it bundled in with Promethean, the other lost orphan child?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:38:08-07:00","id":200723,"title":"","content":"I hope so, either with or without Prommies.<br /> <br /> Not holding my breath though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:46:21-07:00","id":200731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/200712-something-i-noticed-in-the-on-the-horizon-section-of-the-onyx-path-release-list?p=200723#post200723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope so, either with or without Prommies.<br /> <br /> Not holding my breath though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. I'm a little sad by that fact, Geist was the first nWoD book I really read read. Plus the concept is ripe for playing with. I know it's the Orphan splat because it isn't the most popular/people wanted more wraith but then again that doesn't stop Promethan from having more books than geist. Such is the pain of liking the concept of people with an avatar of death connected to them going into the underworld to solve mysteries and shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:52:32-07:00","id":200734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arch-Magos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/200712-something-i-noticed-in-the-on-the-horizon-section-of-the-onyx-path-release-list?p=200731#post200731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's the Orphan splat because it isn't the most popular/people wanted more wraith</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's the &quot;orphan&quot; splat because its run was designed for one/two books and it didn't achieve the degree of popularity that Changeling did to get its limited-line length appended. Hopefully the Ready-Made Characters will help drum up some more interest in the game, but in the meantime there's a handful of SASes and multiple sections in Mirrors and similar bluebooks to draw from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T21:57:54-07:00","id":200738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/200712-something-i-noticed-in-the-on-the-horizon-section-of-the-onyx-path-release-list?p=200734#post200734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's the &quot;orphan&quot; splat because its run was designed for one/two books and it didn't achieve the degree of popularity that Changeling did to get its limited-line length appended. Hopefully the Ready-Made Characters will help drum up some more interest in the game, but in the meantime there's a handful of SASes and multiple sections in Mirrors and similar bluebooks to draw from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks. I thought it just didn't get any because people were like 'Hey this isn't Wraith, I want Wraith.' Though Changeling getting extra stuff isn't surprising to me considering the sheer quality of writing in that book, especially compared to Geist's... weird lack of much to hook you into a concept. Krewes are nice but when you compare them to courts they sort of feel lacking you know? More Sin-Eater factions would have helped but I guess the writers wanted to experiment, and if that was the case more power to them. <br /> <br /> I doubt we'll ever get that update, but yeah, the Blue Books do provide some nice stuff to do with Sin-Eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T00:35:35-07:00","id":200823,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see more Geist, certainly. I am hoping the RMC draws eyes back this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img i